berkeley-principles-4.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P2 (S3): "perceive" is taken as immediately perceived: what is directly present to the mind in sensing in P2 and as perceived by sense in the ordinary way: the house or river itself is what is seen or touched where perceived_by_sense is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S2) does not follow (berkeley-principles-4.logic.r3.sense1)
